course: dictionary
lesson: 3648
title: One word, two jobs
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A fireman is a person whose job is to put out fires and rescue people. Today the usual word is firefighter, because both men and women do this job. Some older books use fireman for a different job, so context helps you know which meaning is right.
explain: «A steam engine had a driver and a fireman, who shovelled coal into the firebox.» The clue is coal and firebox, not hoses. So here a fireman was the worker who kept the fire burning in the engine.
explain: «Cartoons show elephants drinking through the trunk like a straw and blowing water out like a fireman.» The clue is water blown out with force. Here fireman means spraying water hard, like a fire hose. Always test your meaning in the sentence to check it fits.
fact: A fireman is a noun: one fireman, two firemen.
fact: Firefighters visit schools to teach fire safety: smoke alarms, stop-drop-and-roll, and calling 999, 911, 000 or 111, depending on the country.
fact: Steam-train firemen shovelled coal to keep the engine hot and working.
fact: «Fireman Sam» is a famous cartoon character, and a «fireman's lift» is a way of carrying a person over your shoulders.
exercise: «A steam engine had a driver and a fireman, who shovelled coal into the firebox.» What did the fireman do on the steam engine? | Waved a flag and blew a whistle | *Shovelled coal into the firebox | Drove the train | Put out fires with a hose
exercise: Today's usual word for a person who puts out fires is what? | *firefighter | steam engine | fireplace | smoke alarm
exercise: Which phrase means carrying a person over your shoulders? | *fireman's lift | fireman Sam | stop-drop-and-roll | smoke alarm
test: «Cartoons show elephants drinking through the trunk like a straw and blowing water out like a fireman.» In this sentence, blowing water like a fireman means | shovelling coal into a fire | sleeping in a fire station | drinking through a straw | *spraying water hard, like a fire hose
test: Why do people now often say firefighter instead of fireman? | It means the same as steam engine | *Because both men and women do this job | Fire is no longer used in the word | It is a shorter word
exam: Which meaning of fireman fits «A steam engine had a driver and a fireman, who shovelled coal into the firebox»? | Someone who puts out fires with a hose | *A worker who kept the fire burning in a steam engine | A type of fire alarm | A person who rescues children from smoke
